## Summary of Changes

The fix adds support for the `Eqer` interface in the `where` function comparisons in `tpl/collections/where.go`.

### Problem
The `where` function previously fell through to a no-op (returning `false, nil`) when comparing two values whose kinds were not handled by the primitive type switches (e.g., two Page interface values). This made `where pages "Parent" $page` return an empty list, while the equivalent `range pages` + `if eq` worked.

### Solution
Added a `default` case to the equality operator (`eq`, `==`, `=`, empty/no-op) and inequality operator (`!=`, `<>`, `ne`) switch blocks in the `checkCondition` function. When none of the primitive type checks match, the code now falls back to using `compare.Eq()` from the `compare` package, which properly handles types that implement the `Eqer` interface.

### Changes Made
1. Added import for `"github.com/gohugoio/hugo/compare"`
2. Added a `default` case for equality operations that uses `compare.Eq(v.Interface(), mv.Interface())`
3. Added a `default` case for inequality operations that uses `!compare.Eq(v.Interface(), mv.Interface())`

This matches the behavior of the `eq/ne` template functions in the `compare` package, which also use the `Eqer` interface when available.

### Testing
- The specific test `TestWhereWithPageEqualityIssue14777` now passes
- All existing tests in `tpl/collections/` continue to pass
- All tests in `tpl/compare/` continue to pass
- All tests in `resources/page/` continue to pass
